        "original_id": "ab7d8bb5-46d7-509f-8df5-7d3b543ad7e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Baga Sola, northeastern Nigeria, Chad, Niger, northern Cameroon\n- Organizations: Boko Haram, Islamic State West Africa Province (ISWAP), Jamā'at Ahl as-Sunnah lid-Da'wah wa'l-Jihād\n- Facilities: hospital, fish market, refugee camp\n- Topics: refugees, Islamic extremism, terrorism\n\nFacts:\n- Baga Sola has a hospital, a fish market, and a refugee camp.\n- The refugee camp in Baga Sola serves Nigerians and Chadians who fled Boko Haram.\n- Boko Haram refers to itself as al-Wilāya al-Islāmiyya Gharb Afrīqiyyah, meaning Islamic State West Africa Province (ISWAP).\n- Boko Haram also refers to itself as Jamā'at Ahl as-Sunnah lid-Da'wah wa'l-Jihād.\n- Boko Haram is an Islamic extremist terrorist group based in northeastern Nigeria.\n- Boko Haram is also active in Chad, Niger, and northern Cameroon.",
